Z||000002||Alex2004||01-03-2001||12:53 PM||||In the Chilton Manaul, for 86-88 it says horn relay, dome lights, clock, cigar lighter. So if all of those are out, it is probably a fuse. I scanned this page from our Chilton manual <BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1424968&a=10669082&p=36973067&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||4
Z||000003||TheFiero64||01-03-2001||01:25 PM||||If it is your horn fuse then you would have no power overhead light and the lighter socket. If you don't it is the fuse.<P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
